## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of Strategy pattern and runtime extensibility; expects a minimal interface for a router strategy and a registry that supports hot-loading new strategies. It also probes how the router dispatches to handlers asynchronously and resolves potential conflicts when multiple strategies may apply.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern
- Runtime plugin registry
- Decoupled routing logic
- Async dispatch and back-pressure
- Conflict resolution and ordering

## Code Example

```typescript
interface Message { routingKey: string; metadata: any }
interface RoutePlan { queue: string; weight?: number }
interface RouterStrategy { route(msg: Message): RoutePlan[] }

class StrategyRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, RouterStrategy>();
  register(name: string, s: RouterStrategy) { this.map.set(name, s) }
  get(name: string): RouterStrategy | undefined { return this.map.get(name) }
}

class Router {
  constructor(private registry: StrategyRegistry, private active?: string) {}
  route(msg: Message) {
    const strat = this.registry.get(this.active || '');
    return strat?.route(msg) ?? []
  }
}
```

